<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  PyrelandsGround_ScorchableTerrain.xml   RimUtinni: Fire Ecology  2026-09-01
  ============================================================================
  FIRE_ECOLOGY_LOOP_1, unit 3 (part 2 of 2 — AshLadder.xml in
  RimMandrake: SW — Fire Ecology carries the ladder itself; this file is what
  makes the Pyrelands actually MAPGEN with that ground instead of ordinary
  Sand/Gravel/Soil/SoilRich).

  Deliberately NOT a patch on the shared vanilla Sand/Gravel/Soil/SoilRich
  TerrainDefs — those are used by nearly every biome on the planet, and
  giving them Flammability+burnedDef would make EVERY biome's dirt start
  converting to ash, not just the Pyrelands. Scope stays to the one biome
  that opted in: this file repoints ZBiome_Grasslands' own
  terrainsByFertility and terrainPatchMakers entries at RSW_FE_Ground_* (the
  scorchable clones), positionally, verified against the raw donor XML read
  2026-09-01 (zylle.MoreVanillaBiomes 1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/ZBiome_Grasslands.xml):

    terrainsByFertility  li[1]=Sand li[2]=Gravel li[3]=Soil li[4]=SoilRich
    terrainPatchMakers/li[1]/thresholds  li[1]=SoilRich li[2]=Mud
                                          li[3]=WaterShallow li[4]=WaterDeep

  Only the SoilRich threshold inside terrainPatchMakers is repointed — Mud/
  WaterShallow/WaterDeep are the biome's water features, not ground, and stay
  vanilla (a burnt lakebed reads wrong; a burnt hillside doesn't).

  ⚠️ ONLY AFFECTS NEWLY-GENERATED Pyrelands map tiles. A colony already
  built on Ash'karr's frozen Pyrelands tiles keeps whatever terrain its map
  already holds; this patch changes what a FRESH Pyrelands map generates
  from here on. Flagged for the live quicktest, not assumed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>More Vanilla Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/terrainsByFertility/li[1]/terrain</xpath>
          <value><terrain>RSW_FE_Ground_Sand</terrain></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/terrainsByFertility/li[2]/terrain</xpath>
          <value><terrain>RSW_FE_Ground_Gravel</terrain></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/terrainsByFertility/li[3]/terrain</xpath>
          <value><terrain>RSW_FE_Ground_Soil</terrain></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/terrainsByFertility/li[4]/terrain</xpath>
          <value><terrain>RSW_FE_Ground_SoilRich</terrain></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/terrainPatchMakers/li[1]/thresholds/li[1]/terrain</xpath>
          <value><terrain>RSW_FE_Ground_SoilRich</terrain></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
